The compiler must finish a constant before runtime code begins.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    base #I32 = 4
    larger #I32 = base + 2
]

A constant can use another constant that is already available.

It cannot use a runtime variable or call a runtime function.

When a constant expression is invalid, the compiler reports it during the build instead of leaving the failure for runtime.

A compile-time-known `Bool`, including one provided through `$config`, can select an ordinary `if` branch:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    $config
    enabled #Bool = false

    if enabled:
        perform_optional_work()
    ;
]

`$config` before a typed `#` binding feeds the same ordinary `if` and cannot remove
declarations or dependencies. Future structural selection belongs to `$feature`.
